{"A":"Research low-risk copy/allocation reductions in the existing implementation. Pass read-only graph, matrix, and vector inputs by const reference where safe—especially in Prim_ST, deep, coresConjunto, find_min_key, and is_cycle—rather than copying them. Preserve traversal order and output behavior; measure correctness and runtime before and after, including cases that exercise repeated Prim calls and deep recursion.","B":"Research sparse graph storage and Prim/partition costs. Consider replacing the N×N adjacency matrix with deduplicated adjacency lists, while preserving the current ascending-vertex tie and neighbor iteration order that can affect the spanning tree and output. Measure memory and end-to-end runtime on sparse and dense cases; verify disconnected and duplicate-edge behavior remains correct.","C":"Research the path-search hot path. Build a tree adjacency structure once instead of rescanning arvoreGeradora in buscaAresta; consider mutable push/pop path state, an in-path marker, and incremental color counts to avoid repeated history and color scans. Preserve the existing search order, leaf evaluation, early exit, and output formatting, and validate results against the official correctness checks.","G":"Integrate only correctness-checked programs produced by A, B, and C. Benchmark each candidate alone and each proposed combination on the unchanged harness; do not assume gains add, and retain a combination only if its measured end-to-end result improves without losing correctness. Preserve general-input behavior and output formatting; do not alter tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, permissions, or source beyond the candidate changes.","analysis":"The supplied baseline is valid and correct on 4 cases, with mean runtime 0.005705340765416622 seconds and score 0.5. No per-case profiles, other sources, or prior role results are available, so bottlenecks are inferred from the source rather than established by measurement. Likely costs include repeated graph/matrix copies, dense adjacency storage and initialization, repeated Prim/partition work, and recursive path-search scans and copies. The target is ARM64 with 4 cores; given the small measured runtime and no profile, prioritize isolated, semantics-preserving changes and measured end-to-end comparisons rather than assuming parallelism or additive gains."}